# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the engine agrees with native to rel 1e-10 (abs floor 1e-10) in every thermo value and per-atom force and position; 1e-10 is the tightest tolerance measured on these cases.
# oracle: the AMOEBA water box of examples/amoeba (in.water_box.amoeba, data.water_box.amoeba = w119amoeba_box.data, amoeba_water.prm = w119amoeba_water.prm, amoeba_water_box.key = w119amoeba_box_full.key: ewald, ewald-alpha 0.4, pewald-alpha 0.5, pme-grid 24, cutoff 7 taper 6, polar-eps 1e-5, bond class2, angle amoeba, one/five special bonds), 648 atoms, full Ewald summation with the permanent multipoles, the induced dipoles and the polarization, run 0 (energies, forces, press, c_virial).
# oracle-inputs: w119amoeba_box.data w119amoeba_water.prm w119amoeba_box_full.key
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-10
units           real
boundary        p p p
atom_style      amoeba
bond_style      class2
angle_style     amoeba
dihedral_style  none
fix             amtype all property/atom i_amtype ghost yes
fix             extra all property/atom i_amgroup d_redID d_pval ghost yes
fix             extra2 all property/atom i_polaxe d2_xyzaxis 3
read_data       w119amoeba_box.data fix amtype NULL "Tinker Types"
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.5 0.5 0.5 one/five yes
pair_style      amoeba
pair_coeff      * * w119amoeba_water.prm w119amoeba_box_full.key
compute         p all pair amoeba
compute         virial all pressure NULL virial
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl c_p[1] c_p[2] c_p[3] c_p[4] c_p[5] c_p[6] press c_virial[1] c_virial[2] c_virial[3] c_virial[4] c_virial[5] c_virial[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
